Z||000003||GodSend||09-20-2001||02:59 PM||||It is actually very easy to take the seats out to inspect.  Basically there are 4 bolts (although you can not slide the seat around - it should still be possible with an open ended wrench).<P>Once you get them out, just take a look at the mechanism on the underside.  The level basically pulls a wire which releases the lock from the teeth on the slider (hard to discribe , but you will know exactly what I am talking about).  There are a few possibilities here..<P>a]  The wire/spring has come off.  Replace, or reinstall - Easy (check both wires.. the one from handle to slider #1, and from slider #1 to slider #2)<P>b]  The handle is bent.  I have seen this before In a few cars.  It may not be obvious at first because it does not take much.  Pull the level and make sure that the wire pulls the stop completely out of the teeth (again, hard to explain, but easy when you see it).<P>  Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-20-2001||03:52 PM||||Time for a new (or old) tool: BFH- (Big F'n Hammer)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||JetroGT||09-20-2001||05:10 PM||||Check for something in the track. loose change, anything.||||reg||1
